= Autonomy vs Well-being  [VT-01] =

//Two values that cannot both be fully served, documented as the trade-off it actually encodes rather than as an absolute bound.//

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-01
|Name|Autonomy vs Well-being
|Status|In Progress
|Evidence basis|Interviews/observations with residents and care staff
|Values in tension|(((
HV-01 Autonomy: pulls toward allowing the resident to initiate and perform everyday activities independently.

HV-05 Well-being: pulls toward intervening when independent performance may lead to distress, confusion, discomfort, or unsafe outcomes.
)))
|Domain area|safety/physical-environmental
|Nature of the conflict|Giving residents more freedom to perform activities independently supports autonomy, but too little assistance may result in mistakes, confusion, frustration, or unsafe situations.
|Non-negotiable floor|If there is an immediate risk of serious harm, the system must notify caregivers for intervention.
|Current resolution|The situated objective is to support the resident in completing everyday activities as independently as possible while preventing avoidable distress or harm. The conditional function is: IF the resident is able to continue the activity independently, THEN no assistance is provided; IF difficulty is detected, THEN increasingly supportive prompting is provided; IF a safety-critical condition occurs, THEN caregiver assistance is requested.
|Alternatives considered|(((
Immediate assistance whenever difficulty is detected: not preferred because it unnecessarily reduces autonomy.

No intervention unless explicitly requested: not preferred because a resident with dementia may not always be able to recognise or communicate when assistance is required.
)))
|Status of the tension|Provisionally resolved

= Privacy vs Well-being  [VT-02] =

//Two values that cannot both be fully served, documented as the trade-off it actually encodes rather than as an absolute bound.//

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|VT-02
|Name|Privacy vs Well-being
|Status|In progress
|Evidence basis|Interviews/observations with residents and care staff
|Values in tension|(((
HV-03 Privacy: pulls toward allowing the resident to maintain their privacy and personal space.

HV-05 Well-being: pulls toward intervening when independent performance may lead to distress, confusion, discomfort, or unsafe outcomes.
)))
|Domain area|safety and privacy
|Nature of the conflict| Allowing residents to maintain privacy and personal space supports their dignity and autonomy, but too little monitoring may result in mistakes, confusion, frustration, or unsafe situations.
|Non-negotiable floor|none
|Current resolution|Monitor only the information necessary to determine whether support is needed, and avoid sharing sensitive information unless the agreed conditions for caregiver involvement are met.
|Alternatives considered|(((
Constant monitoring of all activities: not preferred because it unnecessarily reduces privacy and dignity.
)))
|Status of the tension|Provisionally resolved

= Value Tension  [VT-03] =

//Two values that cannot both be fully served, documented as the trade-off it actually encodes rather than as an absolute bound.//

**Report Format:** §1.2 Human Values and Human Factors

== Fields ==

|=Field|=Description
|ID|Stable identifier, unique within this entity type (e.g. VT-01, VT-02…).
|Name|A short, human-readable label for this instance.
|Status|Not Started / In Progress / Under Review / In Evaluation / Finalized.
|Evidence basis|How this knowledge was obtained — direct observation, interview, literature, secondary data, or proxy informant — flagged as provisional where it rests on anything other than direct contact with the Stakeholder group it describes. For a Measure or Evaluation Method, cite existing use in a validation study or authoritative literature (e.g. a validated-instrument source or textbook) instead.
|Values in tension|the two (or more) Human Value IDs, and which pulls which way.
|Domain area|safety, privacy, reliability, time-criticality, or physical/environmental.
|Nature of the conflict|why serving one costs the other, concretely.
|Non-negotiable floor|any regulatory requirement or hard safety standard that bounds the trade-off absolutely, with citation. State “none” explicitly if there is none — this field is what prevents a real safety limit being mistaken for an open trade-off.
|Current resolution|how this design resolves it, and the rationale.
|Alternatives considered|other resolutions weighed, and why they were not taken.
|Status of the tension|resolved, provisionally resolved, or open — an open tension is a candidate for a Claim about adverse effects.

== Graph edges ==

involves → Human Value; bounds → (Specification-phase) Function; strained-by → Technology Option.